---
source: sched/tests/help.rs
expression: "help_output(\"ionice\")"
---
Set or get process I/O scheduling class and priority

Usage: ionice [-c class] [-n level] [-t] -p PID...
       ionice [-c class] [-n level] [-t] -P PGID...
       ionice [-c class] [-n level] [-t] -u UID...
       ionice [-c class] [-n level] [-t] command [args...]
       ionice [-p PID...] [-P PGID...] [-u UID...]

Arguments:
  [COMMAND]...  Command to run with the given I/O scheduling

Options:
  -c, --class <CLASS>          I/O scheduling class (0=none, 1=realtime, 2=best-effort, 3=idle)
  -n, --classdata <CLASSDATA>  I/O scheduling priority level (0-7, 0 is highest)
  -p, --pid <PID>...           Process IDs to query or set
  -P, --pgid <PGID>...         Process group IDs to query or set
  -u, --uid <UID>...           User IDs to query or set
  -t, --ignore                 Ignore failure to set the requested priority
  -h, --help                   Print help
